{"ts": 1784343052.2209823, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire episode. This was never wrong-direction: price went favorable almost immediately (frame 1, +2pts) and built to +260pts within ~30 minutes, then oscillated in a wide +150 to +260 range for the rest of the window without ever threatening to give back the bulk of the move or approach breakeven. Several deep-looking pullbacks (e.g. +263 to +148 around t=37-39m) triggered multiple against-fires but each time price stabilized and recovered well above +150, confirming the thesis was intact rather than reversing. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that actually closes below roughly half the peak amplitude with sustained multi-timeframe against-fires and negative lambda across TFs simultaneously -- that combination never appeared here, which is why HOLD was correct throughout.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 43}
